course: dictionary
lesson: 15017
title: Being resourceful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resourceful describes a person who is good at finding quick, clever ways to deal with a problem, using whatever is around them. Resource means something you can use when you need it, so a resourceful person makes good use of what they have.
explain: «When the tent pole snapped, Priya tied two sticks together with string and kept the tent standing.» Priya did not panic or give up. She looked at what was nearby and used it to solve the problem. That is what resourceful means.
explain: To check a word in context, ask: did the character solve the problem in a clever way, using what was to hand? If yes, resourceful fits. Then try the meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Resourceful means good at finding quick, clever ways to deal with problems, using whatever is around.
fact: The forms are resourceful, more resourceful and most resourceful.
fact: Robinson Crusoe is a resourceful character: he builds what he needs on his island.
fact: In the Just So Stories, clever creatures find tricks to get out of trouble.
fact: In safety, a resourceful person keeps calm and thinks about what to do next.
exercise: «Priya tied two sticks with string to hold up the broken tent pole.» Priya is resourceful. What does resourceful mean? | Very loud and noisy | Good at running fast | *Good at finding clever ways to fix problems | Always sad and quiet
exercise: Which of these is an example of being resourceful? | Sitting and waiting for someone to bring a torch | Crying until morning | *Making a lantern from a jar and a candle when the torch runs out | Going to bed in the dark without trying anything
exercise: In a safety drill, what does a resourceful person do? | Forgets what to do and stops | *Keeps calm and thinks of a safe way out | Shouts at everyone else | Panics and runs off alone
test: Which sentence shows a resourceful person? | «Ali cried because his bike was broken.» | «Ali sat down and waited for someone to fix his bike.» | *«Ali fixed his broken bike chain with a piece of wire.»
test: Robinson Crusoe is resourceful. What does he do? | Sleeps all day and forgets his problems | *Builds what he needs from things on his island | Waits for a ship and never tries anything else | Gives up and does nothing at all
exam: Which word best describes someone who finds clever ways to solve problems with the things around them? | *Resourceful | Clumsy | Lazy | Careless
